下面这段可以直接交给 Claude：

```text
Implement the Shaniu Android responsiveness and device-eye interaction improvements below. Preserve all unrelated uncommitted work. Do not commit, push, flash firmware, change keys, or claim real-device acceptance.

Goal

Make the Android app feel immediate while keeping device state truthful:

1. Tapping an expression in Customize should immediately update the local preview.
2. When the authenticated device session is ready, the tap should also start a temporary expression trial on the physical device.
3. The Home eyes must mirror confirmed device state, never pretend that an unconfirmed command succeeded.
4. User operations must not wait behind background polling.
5. Reduce unnecessary UI reconstruction and BLE round trips without weakening the existing BLE + TLS security model.

Implement in two backward-compatible slices.

Slice A — Android responsiveness using the existing protocol

1. Incremental rendering

- Do not rebuild the entire page for every session-state or polling update.
- Keep page views alive while the current page is unchanged.
- Update only the affected eyes, labels, buttons, progress indicators and connection links.
- Coalesce session-state and command-result notifications into at most one UI update per frame.
- A passive poll must not recreate the page, restart entrance animations or reset scroll position.
- Render a new page only when navigation actually changes.

2. Immediate but truthful feedback

For every device action, use three explicit states:

- Pending: show immediately after the tap.
- Confirmed: show only after authenticated device readback or a trusted device event.
- Failed/Timed out: restore the last confirmed state and show a concise error.

Never show pending state as successful.

3. Direct expression interaction

On entering Customize:

- Load the current confirmed expression and trial state.
- Keep the preview available even when disconnected.

When the user taps Daily, Happy or Goodnight:

- Update the local preview within the same UI frame.
- If the device session is authenticated and ready, start the existing 10-second device expression trial.
- Show pending → confirmed → automatically restored, or pending → failed.
- If disconnected, keep it as preview-only and clearly label it as not sent.
- Do not replace the existing explicit action for saving the permanent default expression.

On Home:

- The phone eyes must represent the last confirmed device expression.
- A pending expression may be indicated separately, but must not replace confirmed state.
- Device disconnect or stale state must visibly downgrade confidence.

4. Command scheduling

Classify device requests as:

- USER: direct controls and explicit refreshes.
- POLL: passive background synchronization.

Rules:

- USER requests have priority over queued POLL requests.
- A USER request may cancel a scheduled or queued poll.
- Never interrupt an already in-flight authenticated transaction.
- Do not allow duplicate polling requests for the same state.
- While a user command is pending, perform adaptive confirmation reads approximately every 150–250 ms, with a total timeout of 3 seconds.
- When idle, poll no faster than every 10 seconds unless an existing product requirement needs a shorter interval.

5. Motion timing

Reduce decorative latency while keeping the redesigned visual language:

- Page/navigation transition: approximately 120 ms.
- Tab indicator: approximately 160 ms.
- Bottom sheet: approximately 220 ms.
- Respect the Android “remove animations” setting.
- State confirmation must never be delayed by an animation.

Slice B — protocol optimization, only after Slice A passes

1. Add a compact authenticated display-state message or event over the existing TLS session. It should contain only what interactive UI needs, for example:

- monotonically increasing sequence number;
- confirmed expression;
- trial active flag or trial ID;
- remaining trial time;
- device busy/voice state;
- concise result/error code.

2. Allow the firmware to emit an authenticated STATE_CHANGED event when display, trial, voice, Wi-Fi or busy state changes.

3. Keep polling as a compatibility and recovery fallback.

4. Preserve the existing full eye-package status structure for installation and integrity verification. Do not replace it with the compact interactive status.

5. If transport fragmentation is currently fixed at 20-byte chunks:

- add an explicit capability negotiation;
- use a larger ATT payload only when both Android and firmware advertise support;
- preserve the legacy 20-byte path;
- keep TLS and acknowledged writes for this iteration;
- do not move eye-package downloads from the existing HTTPS path to BLE.

Tests and evidence

Add or update tests for:

- coalesced rendering;
- no page reconstruction caused by passive polling;
- USER requests taking priority over queued POLL requests;
- no duplicate polls;
- pending → confirmed;
- pending → timeout/failure restoring confirmed state;
- disconnect during a command;
- preview-only behavior while disconnected;
- stale or out-of-order sequence rejection;
- legacy 20-byte transport fallback;
- removal of animations.

Run:

- affected Android unit tests;
- assembleDebug;
- instrumentation-test compilation;
- the existing ui_gallery simulated-state test in light and dark mode.

Add emulator scenarios for:

- connected, connecting, disconnected and stale sessions;
- delayed confirmation;
- device rejection;
- timeout;
- disconnect during expression trial;
- rapid expression tapping;
- 20 rounds of tab switching;
- rotation;
- 200% font size;
- remove-animations mode.

Instrument these timestamps without recording secrets:

- user tap;
- request enqueue;
- first BLE write;
- authenticated response;
- device-applied/event timestamp when available;
- UI confirmation frame.

Treat these as target acceptance values, not previously measured facts:

- local visual feedback under 50 ms;
- simple authenticated control p95 under 800 ms;
- device expression visible p95 under 1 second;
- confirmed state reflected in the app within 500 ms after a device event.

Report separately:

1. source review;
2. unit/build results;
3. emulator results;
4. anything requiring a real phone and BK7258 board.

Do not describe emulator or host tests as proof of real BLE or board behavior. At completion, provide the changed-file list, protocol compatibility notes, measured emulator timings, remaining real-device checks and any unrelated pre-existing failures.
```

关于电脑蓝牙：新版 Android Emulator 文档描述了通过 netsim 提供的模拟 Bluetooth Classic/BLE 能力，但这并不等于把电脑蓝牙适配器直接透传给模拟器、连接真实 BK7258。这是根据官方能力描述作出的边界判断。[Android Emulator networking](https://developer.android.com/studio/run/emulator-networking)、[advanced networking and radio simulation](https://developer.android.com/studio/run/emulator-networking-advanced)

Claude 完成后，我会用模拟器验证 UI、状态机、失败/超时和模拟 BLE 会话；真实板子的无线链路最终仍需手机，或者另建主机 BLE 到模拟器的桥接工具。
